{"id": "EUVD-2026-93175", "enisaUuid": "16f31dd2-c17e-32e1-b6f5-7f923b464613", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_codec: validate vendor codec count length\n\nThe Read Local Supported Codecs parsers consume the variable-sized\nstandard codec array before parsing the vendor codec count.  Although the\ninitial reply-size check includes a vendor count byte in the fixed layout,\nit does not guarantee that the byte remains after the standard codec array.\n\nIf a controller reply ends immediately after that array, calculating the\nvendor codec array size reads vnd_codecs->num beyond the skb data.  Use\nskb_pull_data() to validate and consume each codec header before using its\ncount in both command variants.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c04b9a4d08b95dee901d24b7607c4cbd65fa0a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6da782fefae611e68a1aa79644065fc8ca5abcd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4cfd3c4299105237458b27958bd7b0aa4c60795", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f49a543d76d48f184b34225d9c0e2fc4cbdea8ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/12a82819b0cada6e304790b1097f8f9006eb6123", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0795cfd6f655f4de84868a4f4bb41a03f037b3d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w49g-pfqv-m398", "CVE-2026-98247"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06d896cd-5e83-3bcf-978d-e592f0179f66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8961987f3f5fa2f2618e72304d013c8dd5e604a6 <a6da782fefae611e68a1aa79644065fc8ca5abcd"}, {"id": "08880d3f-398d-3acf-9b66-e5806916c02c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "0d321a6f-7e4b-3bd2-8908-0d1283390660", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "106aaedf-3d0d-34bb-89fa-6f698bab5465", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.16"}, {"id": "16693caf-7e84-3cdd-a19c-b621907e9909", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "5eaeb52c-c08d-30f6-88ba-0b584c771e51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8961987f3f5fa2f2618e72304d013c8dd5e604a6 <d0795cfd6f655f4de84868a4f4bb41a03f037b3d"}, {"id": "76232992-57cf-3bef-a862-3817a77f8d95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "979f1d48-a2cf-3567-864e-db7b6b9c6e20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8961987f3f5fa2f2618e72304d013c8dd5e604a6 <e4cfd3c4299105237458b27958bd7b0aa4c60795"}, {"id": "ae7d97e5-f94f-32f9-b6bd-ea4915b7b140", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8961987f3f5fa2f2618e72304d013c8dd5e604a6 <12a82819b0cada6e304790b1097f8f9006eb6123"}, {"id": "b9db9424-6b25-3930-a8b1-69d8ca150861", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c765c2e8-767b-3128-9a5f-a1479ad23d04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8961987f3f5fa2f2618e72304d013c8dd5e604a6 <9c04b9a4d08b95dee901d24b7607c4cbd65fa0a8"}, {"id": "cd7cefea-2daa-3d3a-926f-0b51bbfcc9fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8961987f3f5fa2f2618e72304d013c8dd5e604a6 <f49a543d76d48f184b34225d9c0e2fc4cbdea8ec"}, {"id": "df9cbe8a-29d0-35f3-9f39-4ea76dd7f47d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "e344eb72-1b98-3485-b244-7a71ce9f9565", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7fde9905-1d55-322c-a887-da3a0103392d", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}